   "ONE ARG != \"--a\": gate false, count=15 -> `1`, exit 0. VERIFIED for `notdasha`, `15`, `--A`, `-a`, `--a=15`, `--aa`, `--a0`, `--a 0` (as one arg), `\\xff`.",
   "EMPTY-STRING FIRST ARG `\"\"`: argc==2, `std::string(\"\")` != \"--a\" -> gate false -> `1`, exit 0. VERIFIED: `./test15_executable \"\"` -> `1`. Note argc IS 2 here (an empty arg still counts), but the string compare is what fails.",
   "TWO ARGS, FIRST NOT \"--a\": gate false, argv[2] ignored entirely -> `1`, exit 0. VERIFIED: `15 --a` -> `1`, `--a= 15` -> `1`, `--aa 15` -> `1`, `--A 15` -> `1`, `-a 15` -> `1`.",
   "CASE SENSITIVITY: exact, case-SENSITIVE byte compare. VERIFIED: `--A 15` -> `1` (i.e. treated as non-flag, count stayed 15), whereas `--a 0` -> `0`.",
   "`-a` (single dash) and `--a=` / `--a=15` forms: NOT recognized (no prefix matching, no `=` splitting). VERIFIED: `-a 15` -> `1`, `--a=15` -> `1` (single arg, gate false), `--a= 15` -> `1`.",
   "EXTRA TRAILING ARGS: silently ignored; only argv[1] and argv[2] are ever examined. VERIFIED: `--a 0 99 zz` -> `0`, `--a 15 extra trailing` -> `1`, `--a 0 --a` -> `0`.",
   "`--a` GIVEN TWICE (`--a --a` or `--a --a 15`): argv[1]==\"--a\" passes the gate, then `stoi(\"--a\")` has no digit prefix -> std::invalid_argument -> SIGABRT exit 134. VERIFIED for both `--a --a` and `--a --a 15` (the trailing `15` at argv[3] is never looked at).",
